course: dictionary
lesson: 6718
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for officer. Context, meaning the words around it, tells you which one is meant. «Community police officers visit schools to help children stay safe, not only to catch people.» Here an officer is a police officer, a person whose job is to keep people safe.
explain: Look for clue words next to officer. In «a police officer came round», the word police tells you which meaning to use. In «an officer in charge», the words in charge tell you the officer has an important job in an organisation. Army, navy and air force officers hold a high rank and give orders, so the clue is usually the place or the job.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If «a police officer» means a person who keeps people safe, does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning. If not, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: An officer can be a police officer, a person whose job is to keep people safe and make them obey the law.
fact: In the army, navy or air force, an officer has a high rank and gives orders.
fact: An officer can also be a person with an important job in an organisation, such as a school safety officer.
fact: «Community police officers» visit schools to help children stay safe.
fact: If you are lost in a crowd, a police officer or a steward is a good person to ask for help.
exercise: «Community police officers visit schools to help children stay safe, not only to catch people.» What is the job of these officers? | To hold a high rank in the navy | *To keep children safe and help them | To run the dinner queue at school | To give orders in the army
exercise: «If you are lost in a crowd and there is no meeting point, stay where you are and ask a police officer or a steward.» Which kind of officer is this? | *A police officer | A cook in the school kitchen | An officer in charge of a company | A ship's officer in the navy
exercise: «Community police officers visit schools to help children stay safe.» Find and copy one clue word that tells you which kind of officer is meant. | *police | children | visit | schools
test: «Yes, officer», said Jamie to the police officer who came round. Which meaning of officer fits? | A dog that guards a house | A soldier with no rank who cleans boots | *A person whose job is to keep people safe and make them obey the law | A child who is lost in a crowd
test: The phrase «officer in charge» means: | A soldier who has no rank | A child who has lost their way | A helper in a bright vest at an event | *A person with an important job in an organisation
exam: In «A police officer came round and gave him a warning», which clue words help you find the meaning of officer? | street and Jamie | *police and warning | came and round | Dad and paid
